    "reason": "Let's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: 9 + 2 = 11, write down 1 and carry over 1.\n2. The tens place: 0 + 9 + 1 (carry over) = 10, write down 0 and carry over 1.\n3. The hundreds place: 6 + 1 + 1 (carry over) = 8.\n4. The thousands place: 0 + 9 = 9.\n5. The ten thousands place: 1 + 9 = 10, write down 0 and carry over 1.\n6. The hundred thousands place: 3 + 9 + 1 (carry over) = 13, write down 3 and carry over 1.\n7. The final carry over: 1.",
    "id": "Addition_Q174",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_input": "Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 310609 and 999192?\n# Reasoning:",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "Okay, so I need to add 310,609 and 999,192. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values:\n\n```\n  310609\n+ 999192\n----------\n```\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 9 and 2. Adding those gives 9 + 2 = 11. Hmm, that's more than 10, so I need to carry over. I'll write down 1 in the ones place and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, the tens place. The digits here are 0 and 9, plus the carried over 1. So 0 + 9 = 9, plus 1 makes 10. Again, that's 10, so I write down 0 in the tens place and carry over 1 again.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 6 and 1. Adding them gives 6 + 1 = 7, plus the carried over 1 makes 8. So I write 8 in the hundreds place. No carryover here.\n\nNow the thousands place. The digits are 0 and 9. 0 + 9 = 9. There's no carryover, so I just write 9 in the thousands place.\n\nNext is the ten-thousands place. The digits are 1 and 9. Adding those gives 1 + 9 = 10. Wait, so I write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The digits are 3 and 9, plus the carried over 1. 3 + 9 = 12, plus 1 is 13. So I write 3 in the hundred-thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, that carried over 1 becomes a 1 in the millions place.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,309,801. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carries. \n\nStarting over quickly: 9+2=11 (carry 1), 0+9+1=10 (carry 1), 6+1+1=8, 0+9=9, 1+9=10 (carry 1), 3+9+1=13. Yeah, that seems right. So the final answer should be 1,309,801.\n\n# Answer: 1309801<\uff5c>",
