let me check again step by step to make sure I didn't mix up any digits.\n\nWait, let me do this step by step again carefully:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place: 3 +7 =10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nTens place: 7 +4 =11, plus 1 is 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\nHundreds place:5 +4 =9, plus 1 is 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nThousands place:7 (from first number's thousands place) +1 (from second number's thousands place) =8, plus 1 carried over is 9. Write 9, no carry.\n\nTen thousands place:9 (from first number's ten thousands) +2 (from second's ten thousands) =11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\nHundred thousands place:1 +5 =6, plus the carried 1 is 7. \n\nSo combining all digits: 7 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 0 (ones). So 719,020? Wait, but let me add them numerically without words to confirm.\n\n197,573\n\n+521,447\n\n= ?\n\nLet me add them digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n3 +7 =10 \u2192 0, carry 1.\n\n7 (tens) +4 (tens) =11 +1=12 \u2192 2, carry1.\n\n5 (hundreds) +4 (hundreds)=9 +1=10 \u21920, carry1.\n\n7 (thousands) +1 (thousands)=8 +1=9 \u21929, no carry.\n\n9 (ten thousands) +2 (ten thousands)=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\n1 (hundred thousand) +5 (hundred thousand)=6 +1=7.\n\nSo the total is 719,020. Wait, but let me check with another method. Maybe adding the numbers as whole:\n\n197,573 + 521,447.\n\nLet me break them into parts:\n\n197,573 + 500,000 = 697,573\n\nThen add 21,447: 697,573 +21,447.\n\n697,573 +20,000 =717,573\n\nThen +1,447: 717,573 +1,447 = 719,020. Okay, that matches. So the answer is 719,020. Wait, but let me confirm once more with another approach.\n\nAlternatively, adding 197,573 +521,447:\n\nLet me add the hundred thousands: 100,000 +500,000 =600,000.\n\nThen the ten thousands: 90,000 +20,000 =110,000 \u2192 total so far 710,000.\n\nThousands:7,000 +1,000 =8,000 \u2192 total 718,000.\n\nHundreds:500 +400 =900 \u2192 718,900.\n\nTens:70 +40 =110 \u2192 719,010.\n\nOnes:3 +7 =10 \u2192 total 719,020