    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 520,565 and 280,537. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values:\n\n```\n 520565\n+280537\n--------\n```\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 5 and 7. Adding those gives 12. Hmm, wait, 5 + 7 is 12. So I write down 2 in the ones place and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, the tens place. The digits here are 6 and 3. Adding them with the carried-over 1: 6 + 3 = 9, plus 1 makes 10. So I write 0 in the tens place and carry over 1 again.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 5 and 5. Adding those gives 10, plus the carried-over 1 is 11. So I put 1 in the hundreds place and carry over another 1.\n\nNow the thousands place. The digits here are 0 and 0. Adding them plus the carry-over 1 gives 1. So I write 1 there, and no carry-over yet.\n\nNext is the ten-thousands place. The digits are 2 and 8. Adding those gives 10. Wait, 2 + 8 is 10, right? So I write 0 in the ten-thousands place and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The digits are 5 and 2. Adding them plus the carried-over 1: 5 + 2 = 7, plus 1 is 8. So I write 8 there.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 801,102. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carries. \n\nStarting over quickly: 520,565 + 280,537. \n\nAdding ones: 5+7=12, carry 1. Tens: 6+3+1=10, carry 1. Hundreds:5+5+1=11, carry 1. Thousands:0+0+1=1. Ten-thousands:2+8=10, carry 1. Hundred-thousands:5+2+1=8. Yeah, that seems right. So the total is 801,102.\n",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_answer": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_result": false
  },
