    "id": "Addition_Q316",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_input": "Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 279849 and 370500?\n# Reasoning:",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 279,849 and 370,500. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other to align the digits properly. Hmm, let's see:\n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. \n\nStarting with the ones place: 9 (from 279,849) plus 0 (from 370,500) equals 9. That's straightforward.\n\nNext, the tens place: 4 plus 0 is 4. Still simple.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 8 plus 5. Wait, 8 + 5 is 13. Oh, I need to carry over 1 to the next column. So I'll write down 3 in the hundreds place and carry over 1.\n\nNow the thousands place: 9 (from the first number) plus 0 (from the second) plus the carried-over 1. That makes 10. So I write 0 here and carry over another 1.\n\nNext is the ten thousands place: 7 (from 279,849) plus 7 (from 370,500). Wait, 7 + 7 is 14, plus the carried-over 1 makes 15. So I put 5 in the ten thousands place and carry over 1 again.\n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place: 2 (from the first number) plus 3 (from the second) plus the carried-over 1. That adds up to 6. \n\nPutting all those together, the sum should be 650,349. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carrying over. \n\nWait, let me add them again quickly. 279,849 + 370,500. Adding the thousands: 279,849 + 300,000 is 579,849. Then add 70,500 more: 579,849 + 70,000 = 649,849, then +500 gives 650,349. Yep, that matches. Okay, looks like I did it right.\n",
