    "cot0shot.math teacher_input": "Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 614650 and 540366?\n# Reasoning:",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "Okay, so I need to add 614,650 and 540,366. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. Let me see:\n\n      614650\n    + 540366\n    -----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 0 and 6. Adding those gives 0 + 6 = 6. So I write down 6 in the ones place.\n\nNext, the tens place. The digits here are 5 and 6. 5 + 6 is 11. Hmm, that's more than 10, so I need to carry over. I'll write down 1 in the tens place and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 6 and 3. Adding those gives 6 + 3 = 9, plus the carried over 1 makes 10. So I write 0 in the hundreds place and carry over 1 again to the thousands place.\n\nNow the thousands place. The digits here are 4 and 0. 4 + 0 = 4, plus the carried over 1 equals 5. So I put 5 in the thousands place.\n\nNext up is the ten-thousands place. The digits are 1 and 4. Adding them gives 1 + 4 = 5. No carry-over here, so that's 5 in the ten-thousands place.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The digits are 6 and 5. 6 + 5 = 11. Wait, that's another two-digit number. So I write down 1 in the hundred-thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, that carried over 1 becomes a 1 in the millions place.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,155,016. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carries. Starting over quickly:\n\nOnes: 0+6=6 \u2714\ufe0f  \nTens:5+6=11 \u2714\ufe0f (carry 1)  \nHundreds:6+3+1=10 \u2714\ufe0f (carry 1)  \nThousands:4+0+1=5 \u2714\ufe0f  \nTen-thousands:1+4=5 \u2714\ufe0f  \nHundred-thousands:6+5=11 \u2714\ufe0f (carry 1)  \nMillions:1 carried over. So total is 1,155,016. Yeah, that seems right. I think that's the correct answer.\n\n# Answer:<\uff5c\n\n\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 614650 and 540366?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: 0 + 6 = 6\n2. The tens place: 5 + 6 = 11 (write down 1, carry over 1)\n3. The hundreds place: 6 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 10 (write down 0, carry over 1)\n4. The thousands place: 4 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 5\n5. The ten-thousands place: 1 + 4 = 5\n6. The hundred-thousands place: 6 + 5 = 11 (write down 1, carry over 1)\n7. The millions place: 1 (carry)\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is 1155016.",
