    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "Okay, so I need to add 121,829 and 336,321. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. Let me add the ones digits first. 9 plus 1 is 10. Hmm, wait, that's 10. So I write down 0 and carry over 1 to the tens place. \n\nNext, the tens place. The digits here are 2 and 2. Adding those gives 4, plus the carried-over 1 makes 5. So I write 5 in the tens place. \n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 8 and 3. 8 plus 3 is 11. So I write 1 and carry over another 1. \n\nNow the thousands place. The first number has 1 and the second has 6. 1 plus 6 is 7, plus the carried 1 equals 8. So that's 8 in the thousands place. \n\nNext up is the ten thousands place. The first number has 2 and the second has 3. 2 plus 3 is 5. No carry-over here, so it's 5 in the ten thousands place. \n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place. The first number has 1 and the second has 3. Adding those gives 4. \n\nPutting all the digits together, the sum should be 458,150. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carries. \n\nStarting over quickly: 121,829 + 336,321. \n\nAdding ones: 9+1=10, carry 1. Tens: 2+2+1=5. Hundreds:8+3=11, carry 1. Thousands:1+6+1=8. Ten thousands:2+3=5. Hundred thousands:1+3=4. Yep, that adds up to 458,150. I think that's correct.\n<\uff5c",
