    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 484,957 and 675,457. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other to align the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values:\n\n```\n 484957\n+675457\n--------\n```\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 7 and 7. Adding those together gives 14. Hmm, wait, 7 plus 7 is 14. So I write down 4 in the ones place and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, the tens place. The digits here are 5 and 5, plus the carried-over 1. That's 5 + 5 + 1 = 11. So I put 1 in the tens place and carry over another 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 9 and 4. Adding those gives 13, plus the carried-over 1 makes 14. So I write 4 in the hundreds place and carry over 1 again.\n\nNow the thousands place. The digits here are 4 and 5. 4 + 5 is 9, plus the 1 carried over equals 10. So I write 0 in the thousands place and carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n\nNext up is the ten-thousands place. The digits are 8 and 7. Adding them gives 15, plus the carried-over 1 makes 16. I write 6 here and carry over 1 to the hundred-thousands place.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place has 4 and 6. 4 + 6 is 10, plus the carried-over 1 gives 11. So I write 1 in the hundred-thousands place and another 1 in the millions place.\n\nPutting all the digits together, the sum should be 1,160,414. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes in carrying over. Starting from the right again:\n\nOnes: 7+7=14 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTens: 5+5+1=11 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundreds: 9+4+1=14 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nThousands: 4+5+1=10 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTen-thousands: 8+7+1=16 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundred-thousands: 4+6+1=11 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nYes, that seems right. So the total is 1,160,414.\n",
