s 4 hundred thousands? Let me parse the digits properly.\n\nWait, 670,684 is 6 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 4 (ones).\n\n418,419 is 4 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 9 (ones). Wait, no. Wait, 418,419: breaking down:\n\n- The digits are 4 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 9 (ones). Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo ten thousands place: 7 (from first number) and 1 (from second number). 7 +1 = 8. So that's correct. So the ten thousands digit is 8.\n\nHundred thousands place: 6 +4 = 10. So that gives 0 in the hundred thousands place and carryover 1 to the millions place. So the total would be 1,089,103?\n\nWait, let me add them step by step numerically without the commas to avoid confusion.\n\n670684\n\n+418419\n\nLet me write them as:\n\n  670684\n\n+418419\n\n----------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 +9 =13. 3, carryover 1.\n\n8 +1 =9 +1=10. 0, carryover1.\n\n6 +4=10 +1=11. 1, carryover1.\n\n0 +8=8 +1=9. 9, no carryover.\n\n7 +1=8. 8.\n\n6 +4=10. So 0 with carryover1.\n\nNow, since there's a carryover after the hundred thousands place, we add a 1 in the millions place. So the total is 1,089,103?\n\nWait, let me add them as numbers:\n\n670,684 + 418,419.\n\nLet me compute 670,684 + 400,000 = 1,070,684. Then add 18,419 more.\n\n1,070,684 + 18,419 = ?\n\n1,070,684 + 10,000 = 1,080,684\n\nThen +8,419: 1,080,684 +8,000 = 1,088,684\n\nThen +419: 1,088,684 +419 = 1,089,103. Okay, that matches.\n\nSo the answer should be 1,089,103. Let me check once more with another method.\n\nAlternatively, adding digit by digit:\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically:\n\n\u20036 7 0 6 8 4\n\n+4 1 8 4 1 9\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 4+9=13 \u2192 3, carryover 1\n\nTens:8+1=9 +1=10 \u21920, carryover1\n\nHundreds:6+4=10 +1=11 \u21921, carryover1\n\nThousands:0+8=8 +1=9 \u21929, no carryover\n\nTen-thousands:7+1=8 \u21928\n\nHundred-thousands:6+4=10 \u21920, carryover1\n\nThen the carryover1 becomes the millions place.\n\nSo combining all digits: 1 (million), 0 (hundred thousand), 8 (ten thousand), 9 (thousand), 1 (hundred), 0 (ten), 3 (one). So 1,089,103. Yes, that's correct.\n\nI think that's right. So the final answer is 1,089,103.\n",
