    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 223,806 and 696,963. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. Let me add the ones digits first. 6 plus 3 is 9. That's straightforward. \n\nNext, the tens place. The digits there are 0 and 6. 0 plus 6 is 6. So far, so good. \n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 8 and 9. Hmm, 8 plus 9 is 17. Wait, I need to write down 7 and carry over 1 to the next column. \n\nNow the thousands place. The digits here are 3 and 6, plus the carried-over 1. So 3 + 6 is 9, plus 1 makes 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 again. \n\nNext is the ten thousands place. The digits are 2 and 9. Adding those gives 11, plus the carried-over 1 makes 12. So I write 2 and carry over 1. \n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place. The digits are 2 and 6, plus the carried-over 1. 2 + 6 is 8, plus 1 is 9. \n\nPutting all the digits together, starting from the right, we have 9 in the ones, 6 in the tens, 7 in the hundreds, 0 in the thousands, 2 in the ten thousands, and 9 in the hundred thousands. So the total should be 920,769. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carries. \n\nWait, let me add them again just to be sure. 223,806 plus 696,963. Adding the ones: 6+3=9. Tens: 0+6=6. Hundreds: 8+9=17, carry 1. Thousands: 3+6=9 plus the 1 is 10, so 0 with a carry. Ten thousands: 2+9=11 plus 1 is 12. Hundred thousands: 2+6=8 plus 1 is 9. Yeah, that seems right. I think that's the correct sum.\n",
