    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 665,829 and 674,974. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values:\n\n\u2003665,829\n+674,974\n----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 9 and 4. Adding those gives 13. Hmm, I need to write down 3 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, the tens place: 2 and 7. Adding those plus the carried-over 1 makes 2 + 7 + 1 = 10. So I write 0 in the tens place and carry over another 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 8 and 9. Adding those gives 17, plus the carried-over 1 makes 18. So I put 8 here and carry over 1 again.\n\nNow the thousands place: 5 and 4. That's 9, plus the 1 carried over equals 10. Write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nNext, the ten-thousands place: 6 and 7. Adding them gives 13, plus the 1 carried over is 14. So I write 4 here and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place: 6 and 6. Adding those gives 12, plus the carried-over 1 makes 13. So I write 3 here and carry over 1, but since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes the next digit to the left.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,340,803. Wait, let me check again to make sure I didn't make a mistake in the places. Let me add them another way to verify. Maybe breaking them into parts:\n\n665,829 + 600,000 is 1,265,829. Then adding 74,974: 1,265,829 + 70,000 = 1,335,829, then +4,974 = 1,340,803. Okay, that matches. So the answer should be correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 665,829 and 674,974 is \\boxed{1340803}.\n",
