: Let me check the digits again. Wait, maybe I misaligned the numbers. Let me write them out with place values.\n\nBreaking down each number:\n\n572,745:\n\n- Hundred thousands: 5\n- Ten thousands: 7\n- Thousands: 2\n- Hundreds: 7\n- Tens: 4\n- Ones: 5\n\n334,037:\n\n- Hundred thousands: 3\n- Ten thousands: 3\n- Thousands: 4\n- Hundreds: 0\n- Tens: 3\n- Ones: 7\n\nSo when adding:\n\nOnes: 5 +7 =12 \u2192 2, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 4 +3 =7 +1=8 \u2192 8.\n\nHundreds:7 +0=7.\n\nThousands:2 +4=6.\n\nTen thousands:7 +3=10 \u2192 0 with carryover 1?\n\nWait, ten thousands place: first number has 7, second has 3. 7+3=10. So write 0 and carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands:5 +3=8 plus the carried over 1 makes 9.\n\nWait, so putting it all together:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:2\n\nTens:8\n\nHundreds:7\n\nThousands:6\n\nTen thousands:0\n\nHundred thousands:9\n\nSo the total would be 906,782?\n\nWait, but let me check again step by step:\n\nLet me write each digit's addition:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1. Ones place: 5 +7 =12 \u2192 2, carryover 1.\n\n2. Tens place:4 +3 =7 +1=8 \u2192 8, no carryover.\n\n3. Hundreds place:7 +0 =7 \u21927.\n\n4. Thousands place:2 +4 =6 \u21926.\n\n5. Ten thousands place:7 +3 =10 \u21920, carryover 1.\n\n6. Hundred thousands place:5 +3 =8 +1 (carryover) =9.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are 2,8,7,6,0,9 \u2192 which is 906,782.\n\nWait, but when I first thought I had 915,782? Hmm, maybe I made a mistake in the thousands place earlier. Let me confirm the thousands place again.\n\nWait the thousands digit in the first number is 2 (since 572,745 is 5 (hundred thousand), 7 (ten thousand), 2 (thousand), 7 (hundred), 4 (ten), 5 (one). The second number is 334,037: 3 (hundred thousand), 3 (ten thousand), 4 (thousand), 0 (hundred), 3 (ten), 7 (one). So thousands place: 2 +4 =6. That's correct. \n\nTen thousands place: 7 (from first) +3 (from second) =10. So 0 with a carryover. \n\nHundred thousands:5+3=8 plus 1 is 9. \n\nSo the total is 906,782. \n\nWait, but let me add them numerically to confirm:\n\n572,745 + 334,037.\n\nLet me compute 572,745 + 300,000 = 872,745.\n\nThen add 34,037: 872,745 +34,037 = 906,782. Yes, that matches. \n\nSo the answer should be 906,782. \n\nWait, but in my first reasoning steps, I thought I had 915,782, but that was a mistake. So the correct answer is 906,782. \n\nTherefore, the reasoning steps need to be adjusted accordingly. Let me structure the reasoning properly as per the template.\n",
