    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "Okay, so I need to add 187,277 and 117,501. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values:\n\n```\n 187277\n+117501\n--------\n```\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 7 and 1. Adding those gives 8. So I write down 8 in the ones place.\n\nNext is the tens place. The digits here are 7 and 0. 7 plus 0 is 7. So that's straightforward, write 7 in the tens place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 2 and 5. 2 + 5 equals 7. So another 7 there.\n\nNow the thousands place. Here we have 7 and 7. 7 plus 7 is 14. Hmm, that's a two-digit number. I need to write down 4 in the thousands place and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\nNext is the ten-thousands place. The digits here are 8 and 1, plus the carried-over 1. So 8 + 1 + 1 equals 10. Again, two digits. Write 0 in the ten-thousands place and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The digits are 1 and 1, plus the carried-over 1. 1 + 1 + 1 equals 3. So we put 3 there.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 304,778. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carrying over. \n\nWait, let me add them again quickly. 187,277 plus 100,000 is 287,277. Then adding 17,501 more: 287,277 + 17,501. That would be 304,778. Yeah, that matches. Okay, looks right.\n\n# Answer: 304,778<\uff5c>",
