    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 778,592 and 278,624. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. Let me see:\n\n      778592\n    + 278624\n    -----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 2 and 4. Adding those gives 6. So the ones place of the sum is 6.\n\nNext, moving to the tens place. The digits here are 9 and 2. 9 plus 2 is 11. Hmm, that's more than 10, so I need to carry over. I'll write down 1 in the tens place and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nNow the hundreds place. The digits are 5 and 6, plus the carried-over 1. 5 + 6 is 11, plus 1 makes 12. So I write down 2 in the hundreds place and carry over 1 again.\n\nMoving to the thousands place. The digits here are 8 and 8. Adding those gives 16, plus the carried-over 1 makes 17. So I put 7 in the thousands place and carry over 1.\n\nNext is the ten-thousands place. The digits are 7 and 7. 7 + 7 is 14, plus the carried-over 1 equals 15. So I write 5 there and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The digits are 7 and 2. Adding them gives 9, plus the carried-over 1 makes 10. So I write down 0 in the hundred-thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place. Since there's no higher place, that 1 becomes the millions digit.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,057,216. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carries. \n\nWait, let me add again step by step:\n\nOnes: 2 + 4 = 6 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTens: 9 + 2 = 11, carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundreds: 5 + 6 + 1 = 12, carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nThousands: 8 + 8 + 1 = 17, carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTen-thousands: 7 + 7 + 1 = 15, carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundred-thousands: 7 + 2 + 1 = 10, so 0 with a carryover to millions. So total is 1,057,216. Yeah, that seems right. I think that's the correct answer.\n",
