    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 608,033 and 905,255. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. Let me see:\n\n      608033\n    + 905255\n    -----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 3 and 5. Adding those gives 3 + 5 = 8. So the ones place of the sum is 8.\n\nNext, moving to the tens place. The digits here are 3 and 5. 3 + 5 is 8 again. So the tens place is 8.\n\nNow the hundreds place. The digits are 0 and 2. 0 + 2 = 2. So that's straightforward, 2 in the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the thousands place. Here we have 8 and 5. 8 + 5 equals 13. Hmm, that's more than 10, so I need to carry over. I'll write down 3 in the thousands place and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\nNext is the ten thousands place. The digits here are 0 and 0, plus the carried over 1. So 0 + 0 + 1 = 1. So that's 1 in the ten thousands place.\n\nNow the hundred thousands place. The digits are 6 and 9. Adding those gives 15. So I write down 5 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nFinally, the millions place. There's only the carried over 1, so that becomes 1 in the millions place.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,513,288. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carrying over. \n\nWait, let me add again step by step to confirm:\n\nStarting from the right:\nOnes: 3+5=8 \u2714\ufe0f\nTens: 3+5=8 \u2714\ufe0f\nHundreds: 0+2=2 \u2714\ufe0f\nThousands: 8+5=13, carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\nTen thousands: 0+0+1=1 \u2714\ufe0f\nHundred thousands: 6+9=15, so 5 with carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\nMillions: 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nYes, that adds up. So the final answer should be 1,513,288.\n",
