    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 466,424 and 377,435. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. Let me see:\n\n      466424\n    + 377435\n    -----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 4 and 5. Adding those gives 4 + 5 = 9. So the ones place of the sum is 9.\n\nNext, moving to the tens place. The digits here are 2 and 3. 2 + 3 equals 5. So the tens place is 5.\n\nNow the hundreds place. The digits are 4 and 4. 4 + 4 is 8. That's straightforward, so hundreds place is 8.\n\nMoving to the thousands place. Here we have 6 and 7. Adding those gives 6 + 7 = 13. Hmm, that's a two-digit number. I need to write down 3 in the thousands place and carry over 1 to the next higher place (ten-thousands place).\n\nOkay, the ten-thousands place. The digits here are 6 and 7, plus the carried-over 1. So 6 + 7 = 13, plus 1 makes 14. So I write down 4 in the ten-thousands place and carry over 1 again to the next place (hundred-thousands).\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The digits are 4 and 3, plus the carried-over 1. 4 + 3 = 7, plus 1 is 8. So that's 8 in the hundred-thousands place.\n\nPutting all the digits together, the sum should be 843,859. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carrying over. \n\nWait, let me add them again step by step to confirm:\n\nStarting from the right:\nOnes: 4 +5=9 \u2714\ufe0f\nTens:2+3=5 \u2714\ufe0f\nHundreds:4+4=8 \u2714\ufe0f\nThousands:6+7=13, carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\nTen-thousands:6+7+1=14, so 4 with carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\nHundred-thousands:4+3+1=8 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nYes, that seems right. So the total is 843,859.\n",
