    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 314,771 and 397,845. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The first number has a 1 in the ones place, and the second has a 5. Adding those together: 1 + 5 equals 6. So the ones digit of the sum is 6.\n\nNext, moving to the tens place. The first number has a 7, and the second also has a 4. 7 plus 4 is 11. Hmm, that's more than 10, so I need to carry over. I'll write down 1 in the tens place and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nNow the hundreds place. The first number has a 7, and the second has an 8. Adding those gives 7 + 8 = 15, plus the carried over 1 makes 16. So I write down 6 in the hundreds place and carry over 1 again.\n\nMoving to the thousands place. The first number has a 4, and the second has a 7. 4 + 7 is 11, plus the carried 1 equals 12. So I put 2 in the thousands place and carry over 1.\n\nNext is the ten-thousands place. The first number has a 1, and the second has a 9. 1 + 9 is 10, plus the carried 1 makes 11. So I write 1 in the ten-thousands place and carry over another 1.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The first number has a 3, and the second has a 3. Adding those gives 6, plus the carried 1 equals 7. So that's the hundred-thousands digit.\n\nPutting all the digits together, the sum should be 712,616. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carries. Starting over quickly: 1+5=6, 7+4=11 (carry 1), 7+8+1=16 (carry 1), 4+7+1=12 (carry 1), 1+9+1=11 (carry 1), 3+3+1=7. Yep, that seems right. So the final answer is 712,616.\n",
