    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 223,826 and 792,594. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. Let me add the ones digits first. 6 plus 4 is 10. Hmm, wait, that's 10. So I write down 0 and carry over 1 to the tens place. \n\nNext, the tens place. The digits there are 2 and 9. Adding those gives 11, plus the carried over 1 makes 12. So I write 2 in the tens place and carry over 1 again to the hundreds.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 8 and 5. 8 + 5 is 13, plus the carried 1 makes 14. So I put 4 in the hundreds place and carry over 1 to the thousands.\n\nNow the thousands place. The digits here are 3 and 2. 3 + 2 is 5, plus the carried 1 equals 6. So I write 6 in the thousands place. No carryover here.\n\nNext up is the ten thousands place. The digits are 2 and 9. Adding those gives 11. Since there's no carryover from the previous step, it's just 11. Wait, but how do I write that? The ten thousands place can only hold one digit, so I need to write 1 in the ten thousands and carry over 1 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place. The digits are 2 and 7. 2 + 7 is 9, plus the carried over 1 makes 10. So I write 0 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place. But since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes a 1 in the millions place.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,016,420. Let me check again to make sure I didn't make any mistakes. \n\nStarting from the right: 6+4=10, carry 1. Then 2+9+1=12, carry 1. 8+5+1=14, carry 1. 3+2+1=6. Then 2+9=11, so write 1 and carry 1. 2+7+1=10. Yeah, that adds up. So the final answer should be 1,016,420.\n",
