    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 674,615 and 738,524. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values:\n\n\u2003674615\n+738524\n----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 5 and 4. Adding those gives 5 + 4 = 9. So the ones place of the sum is 9.\n\nNext, moving to the tens place. The digits here are 1 and 2. 1 + 2 equals 3. So the tens place is 3.\n\nNow the hundreds place. The digits are 6 and 5. Adding those gives 6 + 5 = 11. Hmm, that's more than 10, so I need to carry over. I'll write down 1 in the hundreds place and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nMoving to the thousands place. The original digits here are 4 and 8. But don't forget the carried over 1. So 4 + 8 = 12, plus the 1 makes 13. So I write down 3 in the thousands place and carry over another 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n\nNext is the ten-thousands place. The digits are 7 and 3. Adding them gives 7 + 3 = 10, plus the carried over 1 makes 11. So I write 1 in the ten-thousands place and carry over 1 again to the hundred-thousands place.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The digits are 6 and 7. Adding those gives 6 + 7 = 13, plus the carried over 1 makes 14. So that's 4 in the hundred-thousands place and 1 in the millions place.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,413,139. Let me double-check each step to make sure I didn't make a mistake. \n\nStarting from the right again: 5+4=9, correct. 1+2=3, okay. 6+5=11, carryover 1, that's right. Then 4+8+1=13, so 3 with carryover, yes. 7+3+1=11, so 1 and carryover. Then 6+7+1=14. Yeah, that adds up. So the final answer should be 1,413,139.\n",
