    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 679,715 and 344,406. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. Let me add the ones digits first. 5 plus 6 is 11. Hmm, wait, that's 11. So I write down 1 in the ones place and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, the tens place. The digits there are 1 and 0. Adding those gives 1, plus the carried over 1 makes 2. So I write 2 in the tens place. No carryover here.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 7 and 4. 7 plus 4 is 11. Again, I write 1 and carry over another 1.\n\nNow the thousands place. The digits are 9 and 4. 9 + 4 is 13, plus the carried over 1 makes 14. So I write 4 in the thousands place and carry over 1 again.\n\nNext up is the ten thousands place. The digits are 7 and 4. 7 + 4 is 11, plus the carried over 1 equals 12. Write down 2 and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place. The digits are 6 and 3. 6 + 3 is 9, plus the carried over 1 makes 10. So I write 0 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place. But since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes a 1 in the millions place.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,024,121. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carries. Starting from the right again: 5+6=11, correct. Then 1+0+1=2. 7+4=11, so 1 with carryover. 9+4+1=14, so 4 with carryover. 7+4+1=12, so 2 with carryover. 6+3+1=10. Yeah, that adds up. So the final answer should be 1,024,121.\n",
