    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 231,788 and 322,436. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. Let me add the ones digits first. 8 plus 6 is... hmm, 14. Wait, right, that's 14. So I write down 4 in the ones place and carry over 1 to the tens column.\n\nNext, the tens place. The digits there are 8 and 3. Adding those gives 11, plus the carried over 1 makes 12. So I put 2 in the tens place and carry over another 1 to the hundreds.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 7 and 4. 7 plus 4 is 11, plus the carried 1 equals 12. So again, write 2 here and carry over 1.\n\nNow the thousands place. The first number has 1 and the second has 2. 1 + 2 is 3, plus the carried 1 makes 4. No carryover here, so just 4 in thousands place.\n\nNext up is the ten thousands place. The first number has 3 and the second has 2. 3 + 2 is 5. So that's straightforward, 5 in the ten thousands.\n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place. The first number has 2 and the second has 3. Adding those gives 5. \n\nPutting all the digits together, the sum should be 554,224. Wait, let me check again to make sure I didn't mix up any digits. Let me add them another way to verify. Maybe breaking them into parts. \n\n231,788 can be split into 200,000 + 30,000 + 1,000 + 700 + 80 + 8. And 322,436 is 300,000 + 20,000 + 2,000 + 400 + 30 +6. Adding each part:\n\n200k + 300k = 500k\n\n30k +20k =50k \u2192 total so far 550k\n\n1k +2k =3k \u2192 553k\n\n700 +400 =1,100 \u2192 554,100\n\n80 +30 =110 \u2192 554,210\n\n8 +6 =14 \u2192 total 554,224. Okay, that matches. So the answer should be correct.\n",
