    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 386,497 and 426,249. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. Hmm, let's see:\n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. Let me add each column starting from the right.\n\nStarting with the ones place: 7 + 9. That should be 16. Wait, right, so I write down 6 and carry over 1 to the tens place. \n\nNext, the tens place: 9 + 4 is 13, plus the carried 1 makes 14. So I write 4 and carry over 1 again.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 4 + 2 is 6, plus the carried 1 equals 7. No carryover here.\n\nNow the thousands place: 6 + 6 is 12. So I write 2 and carry over 1.\n\nTens of thousands place: 8 + 2 is 10, plus the carried 1 makes 11. Write 1 and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place: 3 + 4 is 7, plus the carried 1 gives 8.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 812,746. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't mix up any digits. Wait, let me add them again just to be sure. \n\n386,497 plus 426,249. Adding the ones: 7+9=16, correct. Tens: 9+4=13 +1=14, yes. Hundreds: 4+2=6 +1=7. Thousands: 6+6=12, so 2 carry 1. Then 8+2=10 +1=11, so 1 carry 1. Then 3+4=7 +1=8. Yeah, that adds up to 812,746. I think that's right.\n",
