    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 987,302 and 629,828. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. Hmm, let me make sure the places are correct. \n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The first number has a 2 in the ones place, and the second has an 8. Adding those together: 2 + 8 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, the tens place. The first number has a 0, and the second has a 2. Adding those plus the carried-over 1: 0 + 2 + 1 = 3. So, I write 3 in the tens place. No carry-over here.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The first number has a 3, and the second has an 8. 3 + 8 is 11. I'll put 1 in the hundreds place and carry over 1 again.\n\nNow the thousands place. The first number has a 7, and the second has a 9. Adding those plus the carried 1: 7 + 9 + 1 = 17. So, 7 in the thousands place and carry over 1.\n\nNext up is the ten thousands place. The first number has an 8, and the second has a 2. 8 + 2 is 10, plus the carried 1 makes 11. So, write 1 in the ten thousands place and carry over another 1.\n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place. The first number has a 9, and the second has a 6. Adding those plus the carried 1: 9 + 6 + 1 = 16. So, 6 in the hundred thousands place and 1 in the millions place. \n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,617,130. Wait, let me check again to make sure I didn't mix up any digits. Let me add them another way. Maybe breaking them into parts. \n\n987,302 is 900,000 + 80,000 + 7,000 + 300 + 2. And 629,828 is 600,000 + 20,000 + 9,000 + 800 + 20 + 8. Adding the hundreds of thousands: 900k + 600k = 1,500,000. Then 80k + 20k = 100,000. 7k +9k =16,000. 300 +800=1,100. 0 +20=20. 2+8=10. Adding all those: 1,500,000 +100,000 is 1,600,000. Plus 16,000 is 1,616,000. Then 1,100 makes 1,617,100. Adding 20 gives 1,617,120, plus 10 is 1,617,130. Okay, that matches. So the answer should be correct.\n",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_answer": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_result": false
  },
