art from the right:\n\n4 +5 =9 (ones)\n\n7+7=14 (tens, write 4 carry 1)\n\n3+6+1=10 (hundreds, write 0 carry 1)\n\n2+7+1=10 (thousands, write 0 carry 1)\n\n6+6+1=13 (ten thousands, write 3 carry 1)\n\n3+6+1=10 (hundred thousands, write 0 carry 1)\n\nThen the final carryover 1 in the millions place. So the number is 1,030,049. Yeah, that seems right. I think that's correct. Let me confirm with another method. Maybe subtract one from the other? Wait, no, addition. Alternatively, use calculator-like approach:\n\n362,374\n\n+667,675\n\n= ?\n\nAdding the numbers:\n\n362,374\n\n+667,675\n\nStart from the right:\n\n4+5=9\n\n7+7=14, so 4 and carryover 1.\n\n3+6=9 +1=10, so 0 and carryover 1.\n\n2+7=9 +1=10, so 0 and carryover 1.\n\n6+6=12 +1=13, so 3 and carryover 1.\n\n3+6=9 +1=10, so 0 and carryover 1.\n\nFinally, the 1 carried over becomes the million digit. So 1,030,049. Yeah, that's consistent. I think that's the correct answer.\n",
