hem another way to confirm. Maybe using another method like expanded form.\n\n547,007 is 500,000 + 40,000 + 7,000 + 0 + 0 +7.\n\n161,640 is 100,000 + 60,000 + 1,000 + 600 + 40 +0.\n\nAdding each part:\n\n500,000 + 100,000 = 600,000\n\n40,000 + 60,000 = 100,000\n\n7,000 + 1,000 = 8,000\n\n0 + 600 = 600\n\n0 +40 =40\n\n7 +0=7\n\nNow add all those together:\n\n600,000 + 100,000 = 700,000\n\n700,000 +8,000 = 708,000\n\n708,000 +600 = 708,600\n\n708,600 +40 =708,640\n\n708,640 +7 =708,647. \n\nSame result. Okay, that seems correct. Maybe I can also use a calculator to check, but since I can't, I'll do another column addition.\n\nLet me write it again:\n\n\u2003547007\n\n+161640\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n7 +0 =7\n\n0+4=4\n\n0+6=6\n\n7 (thousands place of first number) +1 (thousands of second) =8\n\n4 (ten thousands) +6 (ten thousands) =10, so 0 with carryover 1.\n\n5 (hundred thousands) +1 (hundred thousands) =6, plus the 1 carried over is 7.\n\nSo yes, 708,647. I think that's correct. I don't see any errors in my steps. So the answer should be 708,647.\n",
