    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 864,831 and 105,986. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. Hmm, let me make sure the places are correct. \n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The first number has a 1 in the ones place, and the second number has a 6 there. Adding those together: 1 + 6 equals 7. So the ones digit of the sum is 7. No carryover here since 7 is less than 10.\n\nMoving to the tens place. The first number has a 3, and the second has an 8. 3 + 8 is 11. Okay, so I write down 1 in the tens place and carry over 1 to the hundreds place. \n\nNext is the hundreds place. The first number has an 8, and the second has a 9. Adding those gives 8 + 9 = 17. But don't forget the carried over 1, so 17 + 1 = 18. That means I put an 8 in the hundreds place and carry over 1 again to the thousands place.\n\nNow the thousands place. The first number has a 4, and the second has a 5. 4 + 5 is 9, plus the carried over 1 makes 10. So I write 0 in the thousands place and carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n\nMoving on to the ten-thousands place. The first number has a 6, and the second has a 0 (since 105,986 only has five digits here). 6 + 0 is 6, plus the carried over 1 gives 7. So the ten-thousands digit is 7 with no carryover.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The first number has an 8, and the second has a 1. Adding those gives 8 + 1 = 9. There's no carryover here, so that's the final digit.\n\nPutting all the digits together: 9 (hundred-thousands), 7 (ten-thousands), 0 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 7 (ones). Wait, let me check that again. Wait, when I did the thousands place, I had 4 +5 +1 carried over equals 10, so that's 0 with a carryover. Then ten-thousands place was 6 +0 +1 carried over =7. Hundred-thousands place 8 +1 =9. So the digits should be 970,817? Let me verify with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding them step by step:\n\n864,831\n+105,986\n= ?\n\nLet me break it down:\n\nFirst, add the thousands: 800,000 + 100,000 = 900,000.\n\nThen the hundreds: 64,000 + 5,000 = 69,000.\n\nNext, the tens: 831 + 986. Wait, 831 + 986. Let's compute that separately. 800 + 900 = 1,700. 31 +86 = 117. So total is 1,700 + 117 = 1,817. \n\nAdding all parts together: 900,000 + 69,000 = 969,000. Then 969,000 + 1,817 = 970,817. Okay, that matches. So the answer should be 970,817. Let me check once more with column addition:\n\n  864831\n+105986\n--------\nStarting from the right:\n1+6=7\n3+8=11 (write 1, carry 1)\n8+9+1=18 (write 8, carry 1)\n4+5+1=10 (write 0, carry 1)\n6+0+1=7\n8+1=9\nSo yes, 970817. Looks correct.\n",
