ep by step:\n\n800,000 + 130,000 = 930,000\n930,000 + 5,000 = 935,000\n935,000 + 600 = 935,600\n935,600 + 170 = 935,770\n935,770 +7 = 935,777. Okay, that matches my previous result. So that's good. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I should check using another method, like rounding. Let's see:\n\n742,195 is close to 742,200 (rounded up by 5)\n193,582 is close to 193,600 (rounded up by 18)\nAdding those approximations: 742,200 + 193,600 = 935,800. The actual sum is 935,777, which is 23 less than the rounded total, which makes sense because we added 5 +18 =23 to the original numbers. So that checks out. \n\nI think that's solid. So the answer should be 935,777.\n",
