7,712. That's 8,810. Adding all together: 1,300,000 + 140,000 = 1,440,000. Then +8,810 gives 1,448,810. Okay, same result. So probably correct. \n\nWait, but when I first added the ten thousands place: 8 (from 781,098) and 6 (from 667,712). Wait, actually, let me check the digits again. Let me write both numbers:\n\n781,098 is 7 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\n667,712 is 6 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 2 (ones).\n\nWait, so the ten thousands place: first number is 8, second is 6. 8+6=14, so that's correct. Then hundred thousands: 7+6=13, plus the carried 1 makes 14. So the digits are correct. Yeah, so the total is indeed 1,448,810. Alright, I think that's right.\n",
