e original numbers.\n\nWait, 115,254 is 1 (hundred thousand), 1 (ten thousand), 5 (thousand), 2 (hundred), 5 (ten), 4 (one). \n\nSimilarly, 196,136 is 1 (hundred thousand), 9 (ten thousand), 6 (thousand), 1 (hundred), 3 (ten), 6 (one). \n\nSo when adding:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 4 +6=10, carryover 1.\n\nTens:5 +3=8, plus 1 is 9. Wait, wait, in my first calculation I thought 5+3+1=9, which is correct. \n\nHundreds:2 +1=3. Correct.\n\nThousands place: The thousands digits are 5 (from 115,254) and 6 (from 196,136). 5+6=11. So write 1, carryover 1. That's right.\n\nTen thousands place: 1 (from 115,254) and 9 (from 196,136). 1+9=10, plus the carried 1 makes 11. So write 1 and carryover 1. \n\nHundred thousands place: 1 +1=2 plus the carried 1 makes 3. \n\nSo the total is 3 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 0 (ones). So 311,390. That seems correct. \n\nWait, but when I first thought of adding 115k +196k, that's 311,000, and then the remaining 254 +136 is 390, so total 311,390. Yep, that matches. So I think that's correct. \n\nI think my initial calculation was right. So the answer should be 311,390.\n",
