    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 389,192 and 734,382. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. Let me add the ones digits first. The ones digit of 389,192 is 2, and the ones digit of 734,382 is also 2. So 2 + 2 equals 4. I'll write down 4 in the ones place of the answer.\n\nNext, moving to the tens place. The tens digit in 389,192 is 9, and in 734,382 it's 8. Adding those together: 9 + 8 is 17. Hmm, that's more than 10, so I need to carry over. I'll write down 7 in the tens place and carry over 1 to the hundreds column.\n\nNow the hundreds place. The hundreds digit in the first number is 1, and in the second number it's 3. Adding those: 1 + 3 is 4, plus the carried over 1 makes 5. So I write 5 in the hundreds place. No carry-over here.\n\nMoving on to the thousands place. The first number has 9 in the thousands place, and the second has 4. 9 + 4 is 13. So I write down 3 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\nNext is the ten thousands place. The first number has 8, and the second has 3. 8 + 3 is 11, plus the carried over 1 makes 12. So I write 2 in the ten thousands place and carry over 1 again.\n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place. The first number has 3, and the second has 7. 3 + 7 is 10, plus the carried over 1 gives 11. So I write 1 in the hundred thousands place and another 1 in the millions place. \n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,123,574. Let me double-check each column to make sure I didn't make a mistake. \n\nOnes: 2+2=4 \u2714\ufe0f. Tens: 9+8=17 \u2714\ufe0f. Hundreds: 1+3+1=5 \u2714\ufe0f. Thousands: 9+4=13 \u2714\ufe0f. Ten thousands: 8+3+1=12 \u2714\ufe0f. Hundred thousands: 3+7+1=11 \u2714\ufe0f. Millions: 1. Yep, that seems right. So the final answer should be 1,123,574.\n",
