    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 391,106 and 766,404. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. Let's see:\n\n      391106\n    + 766404\n    -----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 6 and 4. Adding those gives 6 + 4 = 10. Hmm, I need to write down 0 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, the tens place. The digits here are 0 and 0, plus the carried-over 1. So 0 + 0 + 1 = 1. I'll write 1 in the tens place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 1 and 4. Adding them gives 1 + 4 = 5. So that's 5 in the hundreds place.\n\nNow the thousands place. The digits here are 1 and 6. 1 + 6 = 7. So 7 goes there.\n\nNext up is the ten-thousands place. The digits are 9 and 6. Adding those gives 9 + 6 = 15. Wait, that's more than 10, so I need to carry over. I'll write down 5 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The digits are 3 and 7, plus the carried-over 1. So 3 + 7 = 10, plus 1 makes 11. So I write down 11 there.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,157,510. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carrying over. \n\nStarting again quickly: 6+4=10 (carry 1), 0+0+1=1, 1+4=5, 1+6=7, 9+6=15 (carry 1), 3+7+1=11. Yeah, that seems right. So the final answer should be 1,157,510.\n",
