n656,747\n\n+306,948\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 7+8=15, write 5, carry 1.\n\nTens: 4+4=8 +1=9, no carry.\n\nHundreds:7+9=16, write 6, carry 1.\n\nThousands:6 (from 656,747's thousands place is the 6 in 6, so wait, let me check the digits again. Wait, maybe I misaligned the digits. Let me write them out with place values:\n\n656,747 is:\n\nDigits: 6 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 7 (ones).\n\n306,948 is:\n\n3 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\nSo when adding:\n\nHundred thousands: 6 +3 =9.\n\nTen thousands:5 +0=5.\n\nThousands:6 +6=12. Wait, so that's 12 in thousands place? Wait, but when adding digit by digit, the thousands place is the fourth digit from the right. Let me confirm:\n\nWait, perhaps I messed up the place values. Let me write each number with commas to clarify:\n\n656,747 is 6 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 7 (ones).\n\n306,948 is 3 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\nSo when adding:\n\nStarting from the right (ones):\n\n7 +8 =15, so 5 with carryover 1.\n\nTens:4 +4 =8 +1=9, no carryover.\n\nHundreds:7 +9=16, so 6 with carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:6 (from first number) +6 (from second number) =12, plus the carryover 1 makes 13. So we write 3 in thousands place and carryover 1 to the ten thousands.\n\nWait, hold on! The thousands place addition: 6 (from first number's thousands) plus 6 (second number's thousands) is 12, plus the 1 carried over from hundreds place gives 13. So the thousands digit is 3, and carryover 1 to the next (ten thousands) place.\n\nThen, moving to ten thousands place: 5 (from first number) +0 (from second) plus the carried over 1 =6. So ten thousands place is 6.\n\nHundred thousands place:6 +3 =9.\n\nPutting all together: 9 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 5 (ones). Wait, that would be 963,695. Wait, but when I broke it down earlier, I thought maybe I made a mistake, but now it's consistent. Let me confirm with another method.\n\nAlternatively, adding 656,747 + 306,948:\n\nLet me add 656,747 + 300,000 = 956,747.\n\nThen add 6,948 to that: 956,747 +6,000 = 962,747; then +948: 962,747 + 900 = 963,647; then +48 = 963,695. Yes, that matches. So the answer is 963,695. I think that's correct. So the reasoning steps should follow that digit-by-digit addition as I first did.\n",
