    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 698,980 and 495,520. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. Let me add the ones digits first. 0 plus 0 is 0. That's straightforward.\n\nNext, the tens place. The top number has an 8 and the bottom has a 2. 8 plus 2 is 10. Hmm, wait, actually, let me check again. Wait, the second number from the right in 698,980 is 8 in the tens place, and in 495,520, the tens digit is 2. So 8 + 2 equals 10. So I write down 0 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The top number has a 9 and the bottom has a 5. Adding those gives 14, plus the carried over 1 makes 15. So I write 5 in the hundreds place and carry over 1 again.\n\nNow the thousands place. The top number has an 8 and the bottom has a 5. 8 + 5 is 13, plus the carried 1 is 14. So I put 4 in the thousands place and carry over 1.\n\nNext is the ten-thousands place. The top number has a 9 and the bottom has a 9. 9 + 9 is 18, plus the carried 1 makes 19. So I write 9 here and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The top number has a 6 and the bottom has a 4. 6 + 4 is 10, plus the carried 1 gives 11. So I write 11 here.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,194,500. Wait, let me verify that again step by step to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nStarting over:\n\n698,980  \n+495,520  \n=________\n\nAdding ones: 0 + 0 = 0  \nTens: 8 + 2 = 10 (write 0, carry 1)  \nHundreds: 9 + 5 = 14 + 1 = 15 (write 5, carry 1)  \nThousands: 8 + 5 = 13 +1 =14 (write 4, carry1)  \nTen-thousands: 9 +9 =18 +1=19 (write9, carry1)  \nHundred-thousands:6+4=10 +1=11 (write 11)\n\nSo combining all digits: 1,194,500. That seems right. Let me check with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts. \n\n698,980 + 400,000 = 1,098,980  \nThen add 95,520: 1,098,980 + 95,520. \n\nBreaking that down: 1,098,980 + 90,000 = 1,188,980  \nThen +5,520: 1,188,980 +5,520 = 1,194,500. \n\nSame result. Okay, that checks out. I think the answer is correct.\n",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_answer": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_result": false
  },
