    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 679,811 and 981,557. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. Let me add the ones digits first. The ones digit of 679,811 is 1, and the ones digit of 981,557 is 7. Adding those together: 1 + 7 equals 8. So I write down 8 in the ones place.\n\nNext, the tens place. The tens digit of 679,811 is 1, and the tens digit of 981,557 is 5. 1 + 5 is 6. So that's 6 in the tens place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The hundreds digit in the first number is 8, and in the second number, it's 5. 8 + 5 equals 13. Hmm, that's more than 10, so I need to carry over. I'll write down 3 in the hundreds place and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nNow the thousands place. The thousands digit of 679,811 is 9, and the thousands digit of 981,557 is 1. Adding those gives 9 + 1 = 10, plus the carried over 1 makes 11. So I write down 1 in the thousands place and carry over another 1 to the next higher place.\n\nNext is the ten thousands place. The ten thousands digit in the first number is 7, and in the second number, it's 8. 7 + 8 is 15, plus the carried over 1 makes 16. So I put 6 in the ten thousands place and carry over 1 again.\n\nNow the hundred thousands place. The first number has 6 in the hundred thousands place, and the second number has 9. Adding those: 6 + 9 = 15, plus the carried over 1 gives 16. So I write 6 here and carry over 1 more.\n\nSince there are no more digits left, that carried over 1 becomes the next digit in the millions place. So the final digit is 1.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,661,368. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carrying over. Starting from the right again:\n\nOnes: 1+7=8 \u2714\ufe0f  \nTens:1+5=6 \u2714\ufe0f  \nHundreds:8+5=13 \u2714\ufe0f (carry 1)  \nThousands:9+1+1(carry)=11 \u2714\ufe0f (carry 1)  \nTen thousands:7+8+1=16 \u2714\ufe0f (carry 1)  \nHundred thousands:6+9+1=16 \u2714\ufe0f (carry 1)  \nMillions:1 \u2714\ufe0f  \n\nYes, that adds up correctly. So the final answer should be 1,661,368.\n",
