    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 142,362 and 188,793. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. Hmm, let's see:\n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. Let me add each column starting from the right.\n\nStarting with the ones place: 2 + 3. That should be 5. Easy enough.\n\nNext, the tens place: 6 + 9. Wait, 6 plus 9 is 15. Oh, right, so I write down 5 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 3 + 7 is 10, plus the carried-over 1 makes 11. So I write 1 and carry over another 1.\n\nNow the thousands place: 2 + 8 equals 10, plus the 1 carried over is 11 again. So another 1 in this column and carry over 1.\n\nNext, the ten thousands place: 4 + 8 is 12, plus the carried 1 gives 13. Write 3 and carry 1.\n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place: 1 + 1 is 2, plus the carried 1 makes 3. \n\nPutting all those together, the sum should be 331,155. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carries. \n\nWait, let me add them again just to be sure. 142,362 plus 188,793. \n\nAdding the ones: 2+3=5. Tens: 6+9=15 (carry 1). Hundreds: 3+7=10 +1=11 (carry 1). Thousands: 2+8=10 +1=11 (carry 1). Ten thousands: 4+8=12 +1=13 (carry 1). Hundred thousands: 1+1=2 +1=3. Yeah, that seems right. So the total is 331,155. I think that's correct.\n",
