place: 7 + 4 = 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place: 9 + 9 = 18 + 1 = 19. Write 9, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 0 + 2 = 2 + 1 = 3. Write 3, no carry.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 8 + 3 = 11. Write 11.\n\nSo combining all the digits: 11 (hundred-thousands), 3 (ten-thousands), 9 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 5 (ones). So that's 1,139,135?\n\nWait, let me check again. Let me add them numerically:\n\n809,727 + 329,408.\n\nBreaking it down:\n\n800,000 + 300,000 = 1,100,000\n\n9,000 + 29,000 = 38,000? Wait, no. Wait, the first number is 809,727, so the breakdown is 800,000 + 9,000 + 700 + 20 +7.\n\nThe second number is 329,408: 300,000 + 29,000 + 400 + 0 +8.\n\nAdding each part:\n\n800k + 300k = 1,100,000\n\n9,000 + 29,000 = 38,000\n\n700 + 400 = 1,100\n\n20 + 0 = 20\n\n7 +8 =15\n\nAdding all those together: 1,100,000 + 38,000 = 1,138,000\n\n1,138,000 + 1,100 = 1,139,100\n\n1,139,100 +20 = 1,139,120\n\n1,139,120 +15 = 1,139,135. Okay, that matches the previous result. So the answer should be 1,139,135. Let me confirm once more with another method.\n\nAlternatively, adding digit by digit again:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 7+8=15 \u2192 5, carry 1\n\nTens: 2+0=2 +1=3 \u2192 3\n\nHundreds:7+4=11 \u21921, carry 1\n\nThousands:9+9=18 +1=19 \u21929, carry1\n\nTen-thousands:0+2=2 +1=3 \u21923\n\nHundred-thousands:8+3=11 \u219211\n\nSo combining: 11 3 9 1 3 5 \u2192 1,139,135. Yes, that's correct. I think that's the right answer.\n",
