    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 276,783 and 626,635. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. Hmm, let me make sure the places are correct. \n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The first number has a 3 in the ones place, and the second has a 5. Adding those together: 3 + 5 equals 8. So the ones place of the sum is 8. \n\nNext, moving to the tens place. The first number has an 8, and the second has a 3. 8 plus 3 is 11. Oh, that's more than 10, so I need to carry over. I'll write down 1 in the tens place and carry over 1 to the hundreds place. \n\nNow the hundreds place. The first number has a 7, and the second has a 6. Adding those gives 13, plus the carried-over 1 makes 14. So I put 4 in the hundreds place and carry over another 1. \n\nMoving to the thousands place. The first number has a 6, and the second has a 6. 6 + 6 is 12, plus the carried-over 1 is 13. So I write 3 in the thousands place and carry over 1 again. \n\nNext is the ten-thousands place. The first number has a 7, and the second has a 2. 7 + 2 is 9, plus the carried-over 1 makes 10. Hmm, so I write 0 in the ten-thousands place and carry over 1. \n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The first number has a 2, and the second has a 6. Adding those gives 8, plus the carried-over 1 equals 9. So the hundred-thousands place is 9. \n\nPutting all the digits together, the sum should be 903,418. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carries. Starting over quickly: 3+5=8, 8+3=11 (carry 1), 7+6+1=14 (carry 1), 6+6+1=13 (carry 1), 7+2+1=10 (carry 1), 2+6+1=9. Yep, that seems right. So the final answer is 903,418.\n",
