    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 335,994 and 847,473. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. Let me add the ones digits first. The ones digit of 335,994 is 4, and the ones digit of 847,473 is 3. Adding those together: 4 + 3 equals 7. So I write down 7 in the ones place of the answer.\n\nNext, the tens place. The tens digit of 335,994 is 9, and the tens digit of 847,473 is 7. Adding those: 9 + 7 is 16. Hmm, that's more than 10, so I need to carry over. I'll write down 6 in the tens place and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The hundreds digit in the first number is 9, and in the second number it's 4. Adding those: 9 + 4 equals 13. But don't forget the carried over 1, so 13 + 1 is 14. So I write 4 in the hundreds place and carry over 1 again to the thousands place.\n\nNow the thousands place. The first number has 5 in the thousands place, and the second has 7. Adding those: 5 + 7 is 12. Adding the carried over 1 gives 13. So I put 3 in the thousands place and carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n\nTen-thousands place next. The first number has 3 here, and the second has 4. 3 + 4 is 7. Adding the carried over 1 makes it 8. So I write 8 there, and no carry-over this time.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The first number has 3, and the second has 8. Adding those gives 11. Since there's no more carry-over, that's straightforward. So 11 in the hundred-thousands place. Wait, but writing 11 there would actually make it 1,1... which might be a problem. Wait, no, actually, each digit is in its own place. Wait, hold on. Let me check again.\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the place values. Let me write the numbers out with their digits:\n\n335,994 is:\n- Hundred thousands: 3\n- Ten thousands: 3\n- Thousands: 5\n- Hundreds: 9\n- Tens: 9\n- Ones: 4\n\n847,473 is:\n- Hundred thousands: 8\n- Ten thousands: 4\n- Thousands: 7\n- Hundreds: 4\n- Tens: 7\n- Ones: 3\n\nSo when adding the hundred thousands place: 3 + 8 = 11. So that's 11 in the hundred thousands place. But since each digit is a single place, that would actually be 1 in the hundred thousands and 1 in the millions place. Wait, right! Because 3 (hundred thousands) plus 8 (hundred thousands) is 11 hundred thousands, which is 1,100,000. So that means we have to carry over 1 to the millions place. But since there's no millions place in the original numbers, the carry-over becomes a new digit at the beginning.\n\nSo putting it all together:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 4 + 3 = 7\n\nTens: 9 + 7 = 16 \u2192 6 with carryover 1\n\nHundreds: 9 + 4 = 13 + 1 (carry) = 14 \u2192 4, carryover 1\n\nThousands: 5 + 7 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carryover 1\n\nTen-thousands: 3 + 4 = 7 + 1 (carry) = 8 \u2192 8, no carryover\n\nHundred-thousands: 3 + 8 = 11 \u2192 so write 1 in the hundred thousands and carryover 1 to millions.\n\nSo the total sum would be 1 (million) 1 (hundred thousand), 8 (ten thousand), 3 (thousand), 4 (hundred), 6 (ten), 7 (one). So that's 1,183,467.\n\nWait, let me verify that again step by step to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAdding each column:\n\nOnes: 4 + 3 = 7 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTens: 9 +7 =16, so 6 with carryover 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundreds: 9 +4 =13 +1 =14 \u2192 4, carryover 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nThousands: 5 +7 =12 +1 =13 \u2192 3, carryover 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTen-thousands: 3 +4 =7 +1 =8 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundred-thousands: 3 +8 =11 \u2192 so 1 in that place and carryover 1 to millions. So the total is 1,183,467. \n\nHmm, that seems right. Let me check with another method. Maybe adding the numbers as whole:\n\n335,994 + 800,000 is 1,135,994. Then add 47,473 (since 847,473 is 800k +47,473). Wait, maybe breaking it down:\n\n335,994 + 847,473.\n\nAlternatively, 335,994 + 800,000 = 1,135,994\n\nThen add 47,473 to that:\n\n1,135,994 + 40,000 = 1,175,994\n\nThen +7,000 = 1,182,994\n\nThen +473: 1,182,994 + 473 = 1,183,467. \n\nYes, same result. So the answer should be 1,183,467. I think that's correct. Let me just do the straight addition again:\n\n  335994\n\n+847473\n\n----------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4+3=7\n\n9+7=16 (write 6, carry 1)\n\n9+4=13 +1=14 (write 4, carry 1)\n\n5+7=12 +1=13 (write 3, carry 1)\n\n3+4=7 +1=8\n\n3+8=11 (write 1, carry 1)\n\nBut since there's a carryover 1 at the hundred thousands place, that becomes a 1 in the millions place. So the total is 1,183,467. Yep, that's consistent. Okay, confident now.\n",
