tting it all together: the millions place is 1, then hundred thousands is 4, ten thousands is 7, thousands is 0, hundreds is 5, tens is 0, ones is 6. So the total should be 1,470,506. Let me check again step by step to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nStarting over:\n\nOnes: 3 + 3 = 6 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTens: 1 + 9 = 10, write 0, carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundreds: 8 + 6 = 14 + 1 (carry) = 15, write 5, carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nThousands: 8 (from first number) + 1 (from second) = 9 + 1 (carry) = 10, write 0, carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTen thousands: 2 + 4 = 6 + 1 (carry) = 7 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundred thousands: 8 + 6 = 14, write 4, carry 1. Then the millions place gets the 1. So yes, 1,470,506. That seems right. I think that's the correct sum.\n",
