    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 857,730 and 133,302. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. Hmm, let me make sure the places are correct. \n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The first number has a 0 in the ones place, and the second number also has a 0 there. So 0 + 0 is 0. That's straightforward.\n\nNext, moving to the tens place. The first number has a 3, and the second has a 0. Adding those gives 3. So the tens digit in the sum will be 3.\n\nNow the hundreds place. The first number has a 7, and the second has a 3. 7 plus 3 is 10. Wait, that's 10, so I need to write down 0 and carry over 1 to the next column. Let me note that down. The hundreds digit is 0 with a carryover of 1.\n\nMoving to the thousands place. The first number has a 7 here, and the second has a 3. Adding those gives 10 again, plus the carried over 1 makes 11. So I write down 1 in the thousands place and carry over another 1. \n\nNext is the ten thousands place. The first number has a 5, and the second has a 3. 5 + 3 is 8, plus the carried over 1 equals 9. So the ten thousands digit is 9, no carryover here.\n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place. The first number has an 8, and the second has a 1. Adding those gives 9. Since there's no more digits or carryover, that's the final digit.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 991,032. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carries. Starting over quickly: 0+0=0, 3+0=3, 7+3=10 (carry 1), 7+3+1=11 (carry 1), 5+3+1=9, 8+1=9. Yep, that seems right. So the answer is 991,032.\n",
