    "id": "Addition_Q304",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_input": "Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 663601 and 265566?\n# Reasoning:",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 663,601 and 265,566. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. Let me see:\n\n      663601\n    + 265566\n    -----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 1 and 6. Adding those gives 1 + 6 = 7. So the ones place of the sum is 7.\n\nNext, moving to the tens place. The digits here are 0 and 6. 0 + 6 is 6. So the tens place is 6.\n\nNow the hundreds place. The digits are 6 and 5. 6 + 5 equals 11. Hmm, that's more than 10, so I need to carry over. I'll write down 1 in the hundreds place and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nMoving to the thousands place. The digits here are 3 and 5, plus the carried over 1. So 3 + 5 = 8, plus 1 makes 9. So the thousands place is 9, and no carry-over here.\n\nNext is the ten-thousands place. The digits are 6 and 6. Adding those gives 12. Again, that's two digits, so I write down 2 and carry over 1 to the next place.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The digits are 6 and 2, plus the carried over 1. 6 + 2 = 8, plus 1 is 9. So the hundred-thousands place is 9.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 929,167. Wait, let me check again to make sure I didn't make any mistakes in the carrying over.\n\nWait a second, let me verify each step again. Starting from the right:\n\nOnes: 1+6=7 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTens: 0+6=6 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundreds: 6+5=11, so 1 carryover \u2714\ufe0f\n\nThousands: 3+5=8 +1=9 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTen-thousands: 6+6=12, so 2 with carryover 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundred-thousands: 6+2=8 +1=9 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nYes, that seems right. So the total is 929,167. Hmm, but let me add them another way to confirm. Maybe breaking them into parts.\n\n663,601 can be 600,000 + 60,000 + 3,000 + 600 + 0 +1\n\n265,566 is 200,000 + 60,000 + 5,000 + 500 + 60 +6\n\nAdding each part:\n\n600k + 200k = 800k\n\n60k +60k = 120k \u2192 total so far 920k\n\n3k +5k =8k \u2192 928k\n\n600 +500 =1,100 \u2192 929,100\n\n0 +60 =60 \u2192 929,160\n\n1 +6 =7 \u2192 total 929,167. Yep, same result. Okay, confident now.\n",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_answer": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_result": false
  },
