, that gives 1,403,732. I think that's correct. Let me confirm with another method. Maybe breaking the numbers into parts. \n\n542,621 can be 500,000 + 40,000 + 2,000 + 600 + 20 +1  \n861,111 is 800,000 + 60,000 + 1,000 + 100 + 10 +1  \n\nAdding each part:  \n500k +800k =1,300,000  \n40k +60k=100,000  \n2k +1k=3,000  \n600+100=700  \n20+10=30  \n1+1=2  \n\nAdding all those together:  \n1,300,000 +100,000 =1,400,000  \n1,400k +3k=1,403,000  \n1,403k +700=1,403,700  \n1,403,700 +30=1,403,730  \n+2=1,403,732. Yep, same result. Okay, that checks out. I think the answer is correct.\n",
