    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 861,773 and 725,549. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other to align the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values:\n\n```\n 861773\n+725549\n--------\n```\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 3 and 9. Adding those together gives 3 + 9 = 12. Hmm, that's more than 10, so I need to carry over. I'll write down 2 in the ones place and carry over 1 to the tens column.\n\nNext, the tens place. The digits here are 7 and 4, plus the carried-over 1. So 7 + 4 = 11, plus 1 makes 12 again. Another carryover. I'll put 2 in the tens place and carry over 1 again.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 7 and 5. Adding those gives 12, plus the carried-over 1 equals 13. So, 3 in the hundreds place and carry over 1.\n\nNow the thousands place. The digits here are 1 and 5. Wait, let me check again. The first number is 861,773, so the thousands digit is 1 (since it's 8-6-1-7-7-3). The second number is 725,549, so the thousands digit is 5 (7-2-5-5-4-9). So 1 + 5 = 6, plus the carried-over 1 makes 7. No carryover here. So I write 7 in the thousands place.\n\nNext is the ten thousands place. The digits are 6 and 2. Adding those gives 8. Since there's no carryover, that's straightforward. So 8 in the ten thousands place.\n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place. The digits are 8 and 7. Adding those together gives 15. So I write down 5 and carry over 1 to the millions place. But since there are no more digits, that carried-over 1 becomes a 1 in the millions place.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,587,322. Wait, let me verify each step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nStarting over:\n\nOnes: 3 + 9 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1.\n\nTens: 7 + 4 = 11 +1 =12 \u2192 2, carry 1.\n\nHundreds:7 +5 =12 +1=13 \u21923, carry1.\n\nThousands:1 +5=6 +1=7 \u21927, no carry.\n\nTen thousands:6 +2=8.\n\nHundred thousands:8 +7=15 \u21925, carry1.\n\nMillions: the carried 1.\n\nSo the total is 1,587,322. Let me check with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\n861,773 + 700,000 = 1,561,773. Then add 25,549 (since 725,549 is 700k +25,549). \n\n1,561,773 +25,549. Let's do that:\n\n1,561,773 +20,000 =1,581,773\n\n1,581,773 +5,549 =1,587,322. Yep, same result. Okay, that seems right.\n",
