    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 746,869 and 982,828. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values:\n\n```\n  746869\n+ 982828\n---------\n```\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 9 and 8. Adding those together gives 17. Wait, right, 9 + 8 is 17. So I write down 7 in the ones place and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, the tens place. The digits here are 6 and 2. Adding them with the carried-over 1: 6 + 2 = 8, plus 1 makes 9. So the tens place is 9, no carryover here.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 8 and 8. 8 + 8 is 16. So I write 6 in the hundreds place and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nNow the thousands place: 6 and 2. Adding them gives 8, plus the carried-over 1 makes 9. So thousands place is 9, no carryover.\n\nNext is the ten-thousands place. The digits are 4 and 8. 4 + 8 is 12. So I write 2 here and carry over 1 to the next place.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The digits are 7 and 9. Adding them gives 16, plus the carried-over 1 makes 17. So that's 7 in the hundred-thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes a 1 in the millions place.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,729,697. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes in the carrying over. \n\nWait, let me add again step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\nOnes: 9 + 8 = 17 \u2714\ufe0f\nTens: 6 + 2 + 1 = 9 \u2714\ufe0f\nHundreds: 8 + 8 = 16 \u2714\ufe0f (carry 1)\nThousands: 6 + 2 + 1 = 9 \u2714\ufe0f\nTen-thousands: 4 + 8 = 12 \u2714\ufe0f (carry 1)\nHundred-thousands: 7 + 9 + 1 = 17 \u2714\ufe0f\nMillions: 1 carried over. So total is 1,729,697. Yeah, that seems right.\n",
