    "id": "Addition_Q281",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_input": "Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 476639 and 617221?\n# Reasoning:",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "Okay, so I need to add 476,639 and 617,221. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. Let me add the ones digits first. 9 plus 1 is 10. Hmm, wait, that's 10. I should write down 0 and carry over 1 to the tens place. \n\nNext, the tens place. The digits here are 3 and 2. Adding those gives 5, plus the carried-over 1 makes 6. So I write 6 in the tens place. No carry-over here.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 6 and 2. 6 plus 2 is 8. So that's straightforward. Write 8 in the hundreds place.\n\nNow the thousands place. 7 and 7. 7 plus 7 is 14. Wait, so I write down 4 and carry over 1 to the next place. \n\nNext is the ten thousands place. The digits are 4 and 1. Adding them gives 5, plus the carried-over 1 makes 6. So that's 6 in the ten thousands place. \n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place. 4 and 6. 4 plus 6 is 10. So that's 10. Since there are no more digits, I just write that down. \n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,093,860. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes. \n\nStarting over: 476,639 + 617,221. \n\nAdding ones: 9+1=10, carry 1. Tens: 3+2+1=6. Hundreds:6+2=8. Thousands:7+7=14, carry 1. Ten thousands:4+1+1=6. Hundred thousands:4+6=10. Yep, that gives 1,093,860. Looks right!\n<\uff5c>",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_answer": "1093860",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_result": true
  },
