8?\n\nWait, but let me add them numerically without the commas to be sure. 627467 + 810161.\n\nLet me add digit by digit again:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 7 +1 =8\n\nPosition 2 (tens):6+6=12 \u2192 2, carryover 1\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):4+1=5 +1=6\n\nPosition4 (thousands):7 +0=7\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):2 +1=3\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):6 +8=14 \u2192 4, carryover 1\n\nPosition7 (millions): 0 +0 +1 (carryover) =1\n\nSo combining all digits from right to left: 8 (ones), 2 (tens),6 (hundreds),7 (thousands),3 (ten thousands),4 (hundred thousands),1 (millions). So the number is 1,437,628. That seems right. Let me confirm with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\n627,467 + 800,000 is 1,427,467. Then add the remaining 10,161: 1,427,467 +10,161 = 1,437,628. Yep, same result. Okay, so the answer should be 1,437,628.\n",
