    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 214,044 and 365,770. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. Let me add the ones digits first. 4 plus 0 is 4. That's straightforward. \n\nNext, the tens place. The top number has a 4 and the bottom has a 7. 4 plus 7 is 11. Hmm, I need to write down 1 and carry over the other 1 to the hundreds place. \n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The top number has a 0, the bottom has a 7. Plus the carried-over 1. So 0 + 7 + 1 equals 8. So that's 8 in the hundreds place. \n\nNow the thousands place. The top number has a 4 and the bottom has a 5. 4 + 5 is 9. No carry-over here. \n\nNext up is the ten-thousands place. The top number has a 1 and the bottom has a 6. 1 + 6 is 7. Still no carry-over. \n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The top number has a 2 and the bottom has a 3. 2 + 3 equals 5. \n\nPutting all those digits together, starting from the ones up, I get 579,814. Wait, let me check again to make sure I didn't mix up any digits. \n\nWait a second, maybe I should write it out step by step to be sure. Let me do that:\n\nStarting from the right:\nOnes: 4 + 0 = 4\nTens: 4 + 7 = 11 (write 1, carry 1)\nHundreds: 0 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 8\nThousands: 4 + 5 = 9\nTen-thousands: 1 + 6 = 7\nHundred-thousands: 2 + 3 = 5\n\nSo combining all those digits: 5 (hundred-thousands), 7 (ten-thousands), 9 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 4 (ones). That makes 579,814. \n\nWait, but let me verify using another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts. Let's break them down:\n\n214,044 can be 200,000 + 14,000 + 44\n365,770 is 300,000 + 65,000 + 770\n\nAdding the hundreds first: 200k + 300k = 500k\nThen the thousands: 14k + 65k = 79k\nThen the remaining parts: 44 + 770 = 814\n\nAdding all together: 500,000 + 79,000 = 579,000; then +814 gives 579,814. Okay, that matches. \n\nAnother way: Maybe using calculator-like addition. Let me add digit by digit again:\n\n  214044\n+365770\n--------\nStarting from the right:\n4+0=4\n4+7=11 (carry 1)\n0+7+1=8\n4+5=9\n1+6=7\n2+3=5\n\nSo the result is 579814. Yep, same as before. I think that's correct. I don't see any mistakes here. The answer should be 579,814.\n",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_answer": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_result": false
  },
