    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 419,189 and 319,036. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. Let me add the ones digits first. 8 (from 419,189) plus 6 (from 319,036) equals 14. Hmm, I should write down 4 in the ones place and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, the tens place. The digits here are 8 and 3. Adding those gives 11, plus the carried over 1 makes 12. So I write 2 in the tens place and carry over another 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 1 and 0, which adds up to 1. Adding the carried over 1 gives 2. So I write 2 there. No carry-over here.\n\nNow the thousands place. The digits are 9 and 9. That's 18. Wait, but there's no carry-over from the previous step, so just 18. I need to write 8 in the thousands place and carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n\nNext up is the ten-thousands place. The digits are 1 and 1. Adding them gives 2, plus the carried over 1 makes 3. So I write 3 there. No carry-over again.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The digits are 4 and 3. Adding those gives 7. Since there's no carry-over, that's just 7.\n\nPutting all the digits together, the sum should be 738,225. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes. \n\nWait, let me add them again quickly. 419,189 plus 300,000 is 719,189. Then adding the remaining 19,036: 719,189 + 19,036. That would be 738,225. Yeah, that matches. Okay, I think that's correct.\n",
