    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 275,605 and 267,379. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. Hmm, let me make sure the places are correct. \n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The first number has a 5 in the ones place, and the second number also has a 9 there. Adding those together: 5 + 9 equals 14. Oh right, I need to carry over the 1 to the tens place. \n\nMoving to the tens place now. The first number has a 0, and the second has a 7. Adding those gives 0 + 7 = 7, plus the carried over 1 makes 8. So the tens digit is 8. No carryover here.\n\nNext is the hundreds place. The first number has a 6, and the second has a 3. 6 + 3 is 9. So that's straightforward, no carryover. \n\nNow the thousands place. The first number has a 5, and the second has a 7. 5 + 7 is 12. Wait, so I write down 2 and carry over 1 again. \n\nMoving to the ten-thousands place. The first number has a 7, and the second has a 6. Adding those gives 7 + 6 = 13, plus the carried over 1 makes 14. So I write down 4 and carry over 1. \n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The first number has a 2, and the second also has a 2. 2 + 2 = 4, plus the carried over 1 makes 5. \n\nPutting all those digits together, the sum should be 542,984. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't mix up any digits. Let me add them again quickly: 275,605 plus 267,379. \n\n200,000 + 200,000 is 400,000. 75,000 + 67,000 is 142,000. That brings it to 542,000. Then 605 + 379 is 984. Yep, that adds up to 542,984. Okay, that matches. I think that's correct.\n",
