ond number:219,737:\n\nOnes:7, tens:3, hundreds:7, thousands:9, ten thousands:1, hundred thousands:2.\n\nSo when adding the hundreds place: first number's hundreds digit is 7, second is 7. So 7 +7 =14, plus the carried over 1 (from the tens place) makes 15. Wait, so that would be 5 in hundreds place, carryover 1. Wait, I think I made a mistake earlier here. Let me go step by step again.\n\nLet me write each digit's place:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 4 +7 =11 \u2192 1, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 8 +3 =11 +1 =12 \u2192 2, carryover1.\n\nHundreds: 7 (from first number) +7 (second number) =14 +1 (carryover) =15 \u2192 5, carryover1.\n\nThousands: 6 (first) +9 (second) =15 +1 =16 \u21926, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:9 (first) +1 (second) =10 +1 =11 \u21921, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:5 +2 =7 +1 (carryover) =8.\n\nWait, so putting it all together:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:1\n\nTens:2\n\nHundreds:5\n\nThousands:6\n\nTen thousands:1 (with a carryover to the next)\n\nHundred thousands:8.\n\nWait, so the total would be 816,521?\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\nWait, let's do the addition step by step:\n\nFirst number: 596,784\n\nSecond number:219,737\n\nAdding:\n\nStart with ones:\n\n4 +7 =11 \u2192 1, carryover 1.\n\nTens:8 +3 =11 +1 =12 \u2192 2, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:7 +7 =14 +1 =15 \u21925, carryover1.\n\nThousands:6 +9 =15 +1 =16 \u21926, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:9 +1 =10 +1 =11 \u21921, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:5 +2 =7 +1 (carryover) =8.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are 1 (ones), 2 (tens),5 (hundreds),6 (thousands),1 (ten thousands),8 (hundred thousands). So the number is 816,521?\n\nWait, but let me verify with another method. Let's add the numbers in parts.\n\n596,784 + 200,000 = 796,784\n\nThen add 19,737: 796,784 +19,737.\n\n796,784 +10,000 =806,784\n\n806,784 +9,737 = 816,521. Yes, that matches.\n\nAlternatively, using another approach:\n\n596,784\n\n+219,737\n\n= (500,000 + 90,000 +6,000 +700 +80 +4) + (200,000 +10,000 +9,000 +700 +30 +7)\n\nAdding each place:\n\nHundred thousands:500k +200k =700k\n\nTen thousands:90k +10k =100k \u2192 total so far 800k\n\nThousands:6k +9k =15k \u2192 total 815k\n\nHundreds:700 +700 =1,400 \u2192 total 816,400\n\nTens:80 +30 =110 \u2192 total 816,510\n\nOnes:4 +7 =11 \u2192 total 816,521.\n\nYes, that's correct. So the answer should be 816,521.\n\nWait, but in the initial step-by-step reasoning, when I first thought through, I had an error in the thousands place. Let me check again the step-by-step addition:\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n  596784\n\n+219737\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:4+7=11 \u2192 1, carryover 1.\n\nTens:8+3=11 +1=12 \u2192 2, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:7+7=14 +1=15 \u21925, carryover1.\n\nThousands:6 (from first number's thousands place) +9 (second's thousands) =15 +1=16 \u21926, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:9 (first's ten thousands) +1 (second's ten thousands) =10 +1=11 \u21921, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:5 +2 =7 +1 (carryover) =8.\n\nSo the digits are 8 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 1 (ones). So written as 816,521. That's correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 816,521.\n",
