    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 653,745 and 317,797. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values:\n\n\u2003653745\n+317797\n----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 5 and 7. Adding those gives 12. Hmm, wait, 5 + 7 is 12. So I write down 2 in the ones place and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, the tens place. The digits here are 4 and 9. Adding them plus the carried over 1: 4 + 9 = 13, plus 1 is 14. So I put 4 in the tens place and carry over 1 again.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 7 and 7. Adding those gives 14, plus the carried over 1 makes 15. Write down 5 and carry over 1.\n\nNow the thousands place: 3 and 7. 3 + 7 is 10, plus the 1 carried over is 11. So write 1 and carry over 1.\n\nNext is the ten thousands place. The digits are 5 and 1. 5 + 1 = 6, plus the carried over 1 makes 7. So that's 7 in the ten thousands place.\n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place: 6 and 3. Adding those gives 9. \n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 971,542. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes in carrying over. \n\nWait, let me add again step by step:\n\nOnes: 5+7=12 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTens: 4+9+1=14 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundreds:7+7+1=15 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nThousands:3+7+1=11 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTen thousands:5+1+1=7 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundred thousands:6+3=9 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nYes, that seems right. So the total is 971,542.\n",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_answer": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_result": false
  },
