    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "Okay, so I need to add 293,577 and 461,153. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. Let me add the ones digits first. 7 plus 3 is 10. Hmm, wait, that's 10. So I write down 0 in the ones place and carry over 1 to the tens place. \n\nNext, the tens place. The digits there are 7 and 5. Adding those gives 12, plus the carried over 1 makes 13. So I write 3 in the tens place and carry over 1 again. \n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 5 and 1. 5 plus 1 is 6, plus the carried 1 equals 7. So I put 7 in the hundreds place. No carryover here.\n\nNow the thousands place. The digits are 3 and 1. 3 + 1 is 4. Since there's no carryover, that's straightforward. So 4 in the thousands place.\n\nNext up is the ten thousands place. The digits here are 9 and 6. Adding those gives 15. Wait, so I write down 5 and carry over 1. \n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place. The digits are 2 and 4. 2 + 4 is 6, plus the carried over 1 makes 7. \n\nPutting all those digits together, the sum should be 754,730. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes. \n\nStarting over quickly: 293,577 + 461,153. Adding ones: 7+3=10, carry 1. Tens: 7+5+1=13, carry 1. Hundreds:5+1+1=7. Thousands:3+1=4. Ten thousands:9+6=15, carry 1. Hundred thousands:2+4+1=7. Yeah, that adds up to 754,730. I think that's correct.\n<\uff5c>",
