    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 489,665 and 273,202. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. Let me add the ones place first. The ones digit of the first number is 5, and the second number has 2 in the ones place. 5 plus 2 is 7. So, I write down 7 in the ones place of the answer.\n\nNext, the tens place. The first number has 6 in the tens place, and the second has 0. 6 plus 0 is 6. So, the tens digit is 6.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The first number has 6, and the second has 2. 6 plus 2 is 8. So, hundreds place is 8.\n\nNow the thousands place. The first number has 9, and the second has 3. 9 plus 3 is 12. Hmm, that's more than 10, so I need to carry over. I'll write down 2 in the thousands place and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\nNext is the ten thousands place. The first number has 8, and the second has 7. Adding those gives 15, plus the carried over 1 makes 16. So, I write 6 in the ten thousands place and carry over 1 again.\n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place. The first number has 4, and the second has 2. 4 plus 2 is 6, plus the carried over 1 makes 7. So, the hundred thousands place is 7.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 762,867. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carrying over. Starting from the right again: 5+2=7, 6+0=6, 6+2=8, 9+3=12 (carry 1), 8+7+1=16 (carry 1), 4+2+1=7. Yep, that looks right. So the final answer is 762,867.\n",
