    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "Okay, so I need to add 171,036 and 616,635. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. Let me add the ones digits first. 6 plus 5 is... hmm, 11. Wait, right, when the sum is 10 or more, I need to carry over. So I write down 1 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, the tens place. The digits there are 3 and 3. Adding those gives 6, plus the carried over 1 makes 7. So the tens place is 7. No carryover here.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 0 and 6. 0 + 6 is 6. So that's straightforward. Hundreds place is 6.\n\nNow the thousands place. 1 and 6. 1 + 6 is 7. So thousands place is 7.\n\nNext up is the ten thousands place. The first number has 7 and the second has 1. 7 + 1 equals 8. So that's 8 in the ten thousands place.\n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place. The first number has 1 and the second has 6. 1 + 6 is 7. So that's 7 in the hundred thousands place.\n\nPutting all those digits together, the sum should be 787,671. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't mix up any digits. Let me add again quickly:\n\n171,036  \n+616,635  \n=  \nStarting from the right:  \n6+5=11 (write 1, carry 1)  \n3+3+1=7  \n0+6=6  \n1+6=7  \n7+1=8  \n1+6=7  \nYep, that gives 787,671. I think that's correct.\n<\uff5c",
