    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "Okay, so I need to add 770,156 and 866,951. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other to align the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values:\n\n```\n  770156\n+ 866951\n---------\n```\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 6 and 1. Adding those gives 6 + 1 = 7. So the ones place of the sum is 7.\n\nNext, moving to the tens place. The digits here are 5 and 5. 5 + 5 equals 10. I'll write down 0 in the tens place and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nNow the hundreds place. The digits are 1 and 9. Adding them plus the carried over 1 gives 1 + 9 + 1 = 11. So I put 1 in the hundreds place and carry over another 1.\n\nMoving to the thousands place. The digits here are 0 and 6. Adding 0 + 6 plus the carried 1 equals 7. So the thousands place is 7, and no carry-over here.\n\nNext is the ten-thousands place. The digits are 7 and 6. 7 + 6 = 13. I write down 3 and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The digits are 7 and 8. Adding them plus the carried 1 gives 7 + 8 + 1 = 16. So that's 6 in the hundred-thousands place and 1 carried over to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes the millions digit.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,637,107. Let me double-check each step to make sure I didn't make a mistake. \n\nOnes: 6+1=7 \u2714\ufe0f. Tens: 5+5=10 \u2714\ufe0f. Hundreds: 1+9+1=11 \u2714\ufe0f. Thousands: 0+6+1=7 \u2714\ufe0f. Ten-thousands:7+6=13 \u2714\ufe0f. Hundred-thousands:7+8+1=16 \u2714\ufe0f. Millions: 1. Yep, that seems right. So the final answer should be 1,637,107.\n",
